---
/** The privacy URL the App Store listing points at: a policy about the app, not about this
 * website, whose own stays at /privacy. */
import Page from "../../../layouts/Page.astro";
import { REPO_URL, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from "../../../lib/nx-link";

const title = "NX Link — Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "NX Link collects nothing. It has no account, no server and no analytics: the app talks to your camera and writes to your photo library.";
---

<Page title={title} description={description} path="/apps/nx-link/privacy">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>NX Link — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 31 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      <strong>Short version:</strong> NX Link collects nothing about you. It has no account, no
      server, no analytics and no third-party code. It talks to one thing — your camera, on the
      camera's own Wi-Fi network — and writes to one thing: your photo library.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. There is no analytics SDK, no crash reporter, no advertising identifier and no
      tracking of any kind. The app has no backend, so there is nowhere for data about you to go.
    </p>

    <h2>Your photos</h2>
    <p>
      Photos and videos are read from the camera over its own closed Wi-Fi network and written to
      your iOS photo library, which is why the app asks for permission to add to it. Nothing is read
      from your photo library, and nothing is uploaded anywhere. Thumbnails are cached inside the
      app's own storage so the grid is quick the second time, and that cache is deleted with the
      app.
    </p>

    <h2>The network</h2>
    <p>
      The app asks for the Local Network permission because the camera is a device on the local
      network and reaching it is the whole function of the app. It connects only to the camera's
      address on the camera's own subnet. It makes no other connections — not for updates, not for
      licence checks, not for measurement.
    </p>

    <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
    <p>
      The app keeps a short technical log on the device, used by its troubleshooting screen so that
      a connection problem can be described precisely. It records what the app asked the camera and
      what the camera answered. It stays on your phone, it is never transmitted, and it is removed
      when you delete the app. You can share it deliberately if you report a problem; that is your
      choice, and nothing happens automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The app is rated 4+ and has no user accounts, no messaging, no purchases and no content from
      anyone else. It collects nothing from anyone, children included.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes, the new version is posted on this page with its date. The app's
      source is public at <a href={REPO_URL}>{REPO_URL}</a>, so any claim here can be checked
      against the code that makes it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>

<style>
  .prose h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.1rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--rx-fg);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose :global(.updated) {
    color: var(--rx-faint);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .prose {
    max-width: var(--rx-max);
  }
</style>
